            "model": "claude-opus-5-5",
            "answer": "The fault was a reversed cell polarity in the `bat_pads` link of `src/bottle.uhd.ts`: it put the leads' red (+) conductor on the board's BAT- pad and the black (-) on BAT+. I swapped the composition back to `{ p1: \"bat_pos\", p2: \"bat_neg\" }`.\n\nI found it by comparing that link with the cable's pin order (`+`, `-`, straight through from the cell's `lead_pos`/`lead_neg`). `npx protoboard check` did not report the swap as an error; its only hint was an extra `HARNESS_ROUTE_STALE` warning on `battery_leads`.\n\nAfter the fix, `check` is back to the expected 0 errors and 2 warnings (the two strapping-pin warnings), and the stale-route warning is gone. I could not run the fault scenarios script \u2014 the command was denied in this session \u2014 so that confirmation is still outstanding.",
