        {
          "trial": 2,
          "host": {
            "durationMs": 28833,
            "turns": 7,
            "costUsd": 0.2189,
            "model": "claude-opus-5-5",
            "answer": "The fault was a reversed cell: in `src/bottle.uhd.ts` the `bat_pads` link composed the board end of the cell leads as `{ p1: \"bat_neg\", p2: \"bat_pos\" }`, which put the red (+) lead on the BAT- pad and the black (-) lead on BAT+. I found it by reading the link against the harness's pin order (`[\"+\", \"-\"]`, straight through), and `protoboard check` pointed at the same link with a `HARNESS_ROUTE_STALE` warning on `battery_leads`.\n\nI swapped the composition to `{ p1: \"bat_pos\", p2: \"bat_neg\" }`, the only change. `npx protoboard check` now gives the expected 0 errors and 2 warnings, with the stale-route warning gone. I could not run the fault scenarios script because the command was denied permission, so that confirmation is still outstanding.\n\nThe model now describes correct wiring, but the bench cap matches the old model: the leads need to be resoldered red to BAT+ and black to BAT-. It is worth checking the board for reverse-polarity damage before reconnecting the cell.",
