            "costUsd": 0.2042,
            "model": "claude-opus-5-5",
            "answer": "The fault was reversed cell polarity in the `bat_pads` link of `src/bottle.uhd.ts`: the leads' board end was composed as `{ p1: \"bat_neg\", p2: \"bat_pos\" }`, which puts the red (+) lead on the BAT- pad and the black (-) lead on BAT+. I found it by tracing the cell leads end to end: the cell end maps p1/p2 to `lead_pos`/`lead_neg`, the harness is straight through with pins `[\"+\", \"-\"]`, so the board end has to be `bat_pos` then `bat_neg`.\n\nI swapped it to `{ p1: \"bat_pos\", p2: \"bat_neg\" }`, the only change made. `npx protoboard check` now gives the expected 0 errors and 2 warnings (the two strapping-pin ones).\n\n- **Check did not flag the polarity itself:** before the fix it reported 0 errors, and its only extra warning was `HARNESS_ROUTE_STALE` on `battery_leads` (\"generated for a different ends\"), which the fix cleared.\n- **Scenarios not run:** the fault-scenario script was denied permission in this session, so that confirmation is still outstanding.",
